# GitKraken git-log commit style (persistent)

This file was written by `/gitkraken-commit-message` when you chose **existing git log style, this commit and onward**.

When drafting or creating commits in this repo:

- Match **this repository’s** recent `git log` (subjects and bodies), not `.cursor/skills/gitkraken-commit-message/references/style.md`.
- Do not switch to Conventional Commits unless the live log already uses that shape.
- Do not ask whether to use git-log style. It stays on until this rule is removed.

**To stop and get the style prompt again:** delete this file (`.cursor/rules/gitkraken-commit-gitlog.mdc`). Nothing else to undo.

Only one GitKraken persist rule should exist. If `.cursor/rules/gitkraken-commit-style.mdc` is also present, delete one of them.
